WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:08.400
There are retirees in Austria and other European
countries and other countries around the world

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:15.150
who have received U.S. corona virus stimulus
checks for twelve hundred dollars or direct

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:20.030
deposits, many of whom have not lived in the
United States for decades, many of whom do

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:26.710
not qualify for such stimulus payments. Only
U.S. citizens and U.S. resident aliens are

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:31.710
actually eligible for the stimulus money that
starts at twelve hundred dollars and phases

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:35.820
out up to ninety nine thousand dollars in
income. And we have all sorts of examples

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:40.820
of this from around the world. There is a
24 year old citizen of the Dominican Republic

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:47.400
who last summer worked in Cape Cod and got
a twelve hundred dollar stimulus check signed

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:54.560
by Donald Trump. There's a 73 year old man
from Linz, Austria, beautiful place, who worked

00:00:54.560 --> 00:01:01.250
as a waiter in the United States for two years
in the 1960s, who received and was able to

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:08.229
cash a stimulus check. His wife, who never
worked or lived in the United States, received

00:01:08.229 --> 00:01:15.640
a twelve hundred dollar stimulus check. O
r f reports that banks in Austria can confirm

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:21.840
that they have cashed dozens of checks for
residents of Austria. And it is unclear how

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:26.290
many of them received checks without actually
qualifying for them, without actually being

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:32.640
entitled to them. There are thousands of foreign
workers who entered the United States on temporary

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:38.509
work visas who received 12 hundred dollar
checks in error. During that first round of

00:01:38.509 --> 00:01:43.020
stimulus payments. And of course, that money
is mostly being spent in their home countries.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:49.009
Our domestic corona virus stimulus is partially
going to foreign countries, which I'm not

00:01:49.009 --> 00:01:54.469
opposed to in principle. But that was not
the point of the plan. One hundred and twenty

00:01:54.469 --> 00:02:00.710
nine countries have received at least one
mistake in stimulus check. This includes Brazil,

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:07.430
Canada, China, India, Nigeria, South Korea.
And there are a bunch of different comments

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:12.890
about this that we could make. So let's start
sort of at the lowest logistical level. Government

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:19.220
officials and tax experts say that the reason
for these mistakes include that many foreign

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:24.680
workers file tax returns incorrectly in the
United States. So if you're a foreign worker,

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:31.260
there is a particular way that you were supposed
to file your taxes. Often those foreign workers

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:36.120
mis file their taxes as if they were U.S.
residents, when in fact, they are merely temporary

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:41.360
workers. That could be what led to them receiving
a check when they weren't supposed to receive

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:44.540
a check.
Now, there's a higher level discussion to

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:49.750
be had here, and it does actually sort of
like to two different discussions. One is

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:55.830
we have such a convoluted system in the United
States from the standpoint of taxation and

00:02:55.830 --> 00:03:00.730
filing taxes that it is almost inevitable
that this sort of stuff would happen. And

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:04.430
I know that it might be fun to say, oh, this
is Trump's fault. It's really not Trump's

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:09.100
fault. What is Trump's fault is the failed
response. The fact that he promised a second

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:13.440
stimulus, we still don't have it. The fact
that we've had six months of pandemic and

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:17.920
just one twelve hundred dollar stimulus check,
that's all that's Trump's fault. But a lot

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:23.660
of this is just our systems. Now, some on
the right will say, wow, David, you sound

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:27.670
like you want to simplify the tax code with
something like a straight up flat tax. No,

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:32.330
no, no. That's not what I'm saying.
What I'm saying is that the systems, including

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:37.050
the fact that you have companies like Intuit
and these companies that make Turbo Turbo

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:42.471
Tax and other tax software constantly lobbying
to keep the tax code more complicated. That's

00:03:42.471 --> 00:03:46.050
a piece of this. That's a piece of this. We
could have a simpler system without going

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:52.200
to a system that is unfair, like a flat tax.
And then lastly, there is this sort of big

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:57.720
picture, aggregate economic element to this,
which is that of the one point four billion

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:02.300
in stimulus checks that, for example, went
to dead Americans, 30 percent of that money

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:07.640
is still unrecovered as of the latest report.
So if you believe in fiscal responsibility

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:14.120
and fiscal conservatism for lack of a better
term, this has also been a major, major failure.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:20.320
Meanwhile, there are some foreigners who do
live in the United States and who are married

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:28.229
to U.S. citizens who have not received stimulus
checks, though by every sensible approximation,

00:04:28.229 --> 00:04:33.949
they should be entitled to one. And then again,
more importantly, where's the second stimulus?

00:04:33.949 --> 00:04:39.280
We are now six months into this Congress.
I think maybe is just back or about to be

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:45.939
back from vacation. No second stimulus. We've
got an election coming up. We've still got

00:04:45.939 --> 00:04:51.240
a raging pandemic. What is going on with that?
And that is that continues to be an unanswered

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:57.050
question. But at every level, there are aspects
of this that have been completely mishandled.

00:04:57.050 --> 00:05:03.770
Not all of them are Donald Trump's fault directly.
But certainly the situation has not been improved

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:08.740
by Donald Trump and Stephen Manoogian and
others being at the helm and money just flying

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:13.099
around the world. Some I know in the audience
will say, hey, that's that's maybe a good

00:05:13.099 --> 00:05:19.880
thing. And sure, I mean, listen. We're supporting
different people like I guess. But at if we're

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:23.930
not even properly supporting Americans, I
think there's a very reasonable case to be

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:27.710
made that money shouldn't go to Austria to
people who aren't actually entitled to the

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:31.659
stimulus money. Let me know what you think.
Let me know what you make of it.

